      "statusChangeID": "5f1ba28a21b5847827ad529b",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "This is intentional behavior. Buttons are not meant to be held down-- they are more of a \"momentary switch\" than a button. This is a change from previously documented behavior, which is probably the source of confusion.\nThe non-puppet controls use a slower sync than puppet sync, so we can't really trust Buttons for this role. Use a Puppet menu for this purpose.\nHOWEVER, this is good feedback-- you want a quick way to hold something \"on\" for a set period of time. We're taking this into consideration for future additions and controls.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
